    "content": "\"European\" refers to people, cultures, or things originating from the continent of Europe. It often denotes the 27-member European Union (EU), a political and economic union covering over 450 million people and promoting peace, stability, and a common market. The EU uses a common currency (the Euro) in most member states. Key Aspects of \"European\" Context: Definition: A native, inhabitant, or descendant of Europe. European Union (EU): A supranational political and economic entity established post-WWII (1951) to prevent conflict and foster economic cooperation. Geography: Europe is bordered by the Arctic Ocean (north), Atlantic Ocean (west), and Mediterranean Sea (south). Culture: A diverse, rich collection of cultures, languages, and histories. Institutions: Key bodies include the European Parliament, Council of the European Union, and the Court of Justice of the European Union (CJEU). Eurozone: 21 of the 27 EU countries use the euro as their currency, such as France, Germany, Italy, and Spain. The European Union operates on a system of treaties and promotes democracy, rule of law, and economic integration.",
